@startuml
title UML sequence behaviour — Entries are deleted at 2 years
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ArrowColor #344054
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #344054
  FontColor #101828
}
skinparam package {
  BorderColor #667085
  FontColor #101828
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
}
box "Backend — Popkin Worker" #FFF4E5
  participant "PurgeOldAuditEntriesJob" as job
end box
box "Backend — Popkin Application and Domain" #ECFDF3
  participant "PurgeOldAuditEntriesCommandHandler" as handler
end box
box "Backend — Popkin Infrastructure" #FFF4E5
  participant "AppDbContext" as ctx
  database "Popkin database" as db
end box
job -> handler : Daily tick: Send PurgeOldAuditEntriesCommand
handler -> db : Entries with At <= now - 2 years, in batches of 1,000
loop while a batch is found
  handler -> ctx : RemoveRange(batch)
  ctx -> ctx : Allowed: every entry is at least 2 years old (L2-120 AC6)
  ctx -> db : Delete the batch
end
handler --> job : Count deleted (metric, no names)
note over job : No API endpoint updates or deletes an entry;\nAppDbContext refuses an update always, and a delete younger than 2 years
@enduml
